### Create a New Run [POST]

You can create a new run of a workflow using this action. It takes a JSON
object containing a collection of optional run properties along with a required checklist_id parameter.

In cases where the workflow uses role based assignments, roles can be resolved to users using the roles_to_users parameter with the following format:
```{ "0": { "role_id": 15371, "user_id": 95918 }, "1": {"role_id": 2747, "user_id": 9191 }, ... }```
where `role_id` is the id of the role you want to resolve, and `user_id` is the id of the user that the role will be resolved to. The role's id can be get using [get workflow details endpoint](https://manifestlyapi.docs.apiary.io/#reference/0/workflow/get-workflow-details) and the user's id can be get with the [list all users endpoint](https://manifestlyapi.docs.apiary.io/#reference/0/users-collection/list-all-users).

Also, when the workflow collects data. You can pre-populate the step data within the runs using the `data_choices` parameter with the following format:
```{"0":{"data_setting_id":"144","data":"The actual data"},"1":{"data_setting_id":"145","data":"www.manifest.ly"}, ... }```
where `data_setting_id` is the id of the data setting object, and `data` is the actual data that will be set. The role and data settings IDs can be get using the [get workflow details endpoint](https://manifestlyapi.docs.apiary.io/#reference/0/workflow/get-workflow-details). Or using the web app, click to view the workflow settings.

+ Parameters
    + api_key - Your API key

+ Request (application/json)

        {
            "checklist_id": 2034,
            "title": "My new run",
            "late_at": "2021-12-06T22:02:21.186Z",
            "users": [111,112],
            "channel": "a_slack_channel",
            "external_id": "1234",
            "started_at": "2021-11-08T22:05:01.186Z",
            "tag_list": ["tag one", "tag two", "tag three"],
            "roles_to_users": {"0": { "role_id": 300, "user_id": 111 }},
            "data_choices": {"0": { "data_setting_id": 707, "data": 'John Doe' }},
            "notes": "You can add notes to a run for more directions to users"
        }

+ Response 201 (application/json)

    + Body

            {
              "run": {
                "archive_url": "https://www.manifest.ly/runs/archives/ecfad026f4f25880282a6ad24b4fa8b3.pdf",
                "checklist_id": 97,
                "checklist_title": "Blog Promotion",
